## Why This Is Asked

Demonstrates understanding of idempotency, integration testing with external services, and failure scenarios, critical for order processing systems.

## Key Concepts

- Idempotent operations, idempotency keys
- End-to-end orchestration across REST, payment gateway, and warehouse
- Partial failure handling, retries, backoff
- Contract testing, chaos engineering, observability
- Test data management, data store consistency

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example test illustrating idempotent POST /orders
const res1 = await request(app).post('/orders')
  .set('Idempotency-Key','abc-123')
  .send({ items:[{sku:'SKU1',qty:1}], customerId:'C100' });

const res2 = await request(app).post('/orders')
  .set('Idempotency-Key','abc-123')
  .send({ items:[{sku:'SKU1',qty:1}], customerId:'C100' });

expect(res1.status).toBe(202);
expect(res2.status).toBe(200);
expect(res2.body.orderId).toBe(res1.body.orderId);
```

